# Batch files MUST be CRLF. A .bat with bare LF endings misbehaves around
# labels and goto in Command Prompt, and that is not something to discover on
# a borrowed laptop. git archive honours this, so the ZIP really does get CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.inf text eol=crlf
*.txt text eol=crlf

*.md  text eol=lf
